1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,276
Welcome to Daily Brief.

2
00:00:02,226 --> 00:00:05,964
It's Friday, November 20th, 2026.

3
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:08,630
Three stories in about three minutes.

4
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:11,892
First, the chip story everyone is watching.

5
00:00:11,892 --> 00:00:22,095
Nvidia has stopped shipping its H200 artificial intelligence chips to China, even though Washington had given it the green light to sell a version of that model to the country last year.

6
00:00:22,095 --> 00:00:25,714
The company has now decided to pull back entirely.

7
00:00:25,714 --> 00:00:35,380
Analysts say the move shows how fragile the trade truce between the two countries still is, and how quickly the rules of the game can change for the world's most valuable chipmaker.

8
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,845
Second, the economic numbers from South Korea.

9
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:49,916
The country has just passed the one trillion dollar mark in annual exports for the first time, and a huge amount of that growth comes from one thing: memory chips built for artificial intelligence.

10
00:00:49,916 --> 00:00:56,869
Samsung and SK Hynix are both riding this wave, as global tech companies pour money into data centres.

11
00:00:56,869 --> 00:00:59,190
But there is a warning attached.

12
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:06,821
South Korean officials say the boom is concentrated, and if spending on AI slows, the country could feel the shock more than most.

13
00:01:06,821 --> 00:01:09,726
Third, a quiet but important meeting.

14
00:01:09,726 --> 00:01:17,511
Leaders from China, Russia and the United States held a trilateral summit on the sidelines of the APEC leaders meeting this week.

15
00:01:17,511 --> 00:01:24,904
International media are calling it significant, and officials on several continents say the signals from the meeting were positive.

16
00:01:24,904 --> 00:01:30,630
Details are still thin, but the fact that the three met at all is being read as a shift in tone.

17
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:32,857
That's your briefing for today.

18
00:01:32,857 --> 00:01:37,107
If you want to read along, the full transcript is in the show notes.

19
00:01:37,107 --> 00:01:39,321
I'll be back tomorrow morning.

